WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:08.650
Various systems and organizations exist to facilitate everyday activities in space.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:09.780
Pirates,

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.700
and the insurance unions that support them, are one example.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.850
After the war for independence,

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.950
and annexation by the Galactic Empire,

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.370
the times move onward, from stormy seas to calm.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.500
Pirates and insurance companies are now joined at the hip.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:26.960
And...

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.010
There are lots of people you trust who can pilot a spaceship, right?

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.010
No way!

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.940
Isolation Ward
No Admittance

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.110
Blue ribbons!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.530
I win.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.690
S-Seriously?

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.320
Kane wins again?

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.160
Damn it!

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:24.040
I guess that bottle of scotch stays with me.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:24.830
One more...

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.290
One more round!

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.120
Hey, Misa...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.040
Think we should contact Marika soon?

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.840
Her yacht club practice cruise starts today.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.510
Practice cruise?

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.260
Yeah, she said it was a last-minute thing.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.800
Well, being on a ship will help keep her from getting rusty.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.970
I wanna get back out there, in the sky...

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.810
I'm gonna lose my edge here.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.650
It's just for a while. Stay strong.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.190
Perhaps not.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:57.650
But what will they do about a navigator's license?

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.280
Did they find a new advisor?

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:01.740
She didn't say...

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.280
But Marika's licensed, so it'll be fine.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.210
This is the Sea of the Morningstar Relay Station Control Tower.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.880
Odette II, you are cleared for launch.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.710
Thank you.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.760
I hope everything keeps going smoothly at the relay station.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.760
You have a nice journey, as well, Captain McDougal.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:24.350
We're cleared for launch!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.390
Great job, President.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:29.980
The control tower never suspected a thing.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.020
This is Captain Kane McDougal.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.570
Wow... Hard to believe that's a dummy.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.030
Way to go, President!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.220
We'll call you Cracker O'Lynn!

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.490
Hey! Don't give me weird names!

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.160
Right...

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.370
We will now begin the Odette II's practice cruise.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.290
This time, we will be performing some pirating duties as well.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.130
Everyone, stay sharp.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.630
And overseeing everything

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.760
will be Kato Marika, captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.800
Keep that in mind, okay?

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:03.720
Right!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.430
Let's do this, everyone.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.390
I guess Marika's in space now...

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.150
Chiaki also left on the cruise

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.360
right after she transferred.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.190
Mami, you should join the yacht club too.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:20.480
I'm fine.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.110
The port's good enough for me.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.140
Welcome!

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.540
Kato Ririka
Resume:

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.200
Here, the house blend.
Kato Ririka
Resume:

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.580
Thank you.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.000
What's that?

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.420
Oh, I'm considering switching careers.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.460
Marika's doing so much, and felt compelled to as well.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.840
I know the feeling!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:47.930
You want to do what you can, don't you?

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.720
Maybe that's why everyone follows Marika...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.730
Chiaki, the princess, and me too.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:59.190
I've taught her many things to make her a good captain.

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.650
Being able to say that makes me happy, as a mother.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.080
Confirming course.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.920
Here is the Odette II's flight plan, as submitted to the control tower.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.300
We skirt around the Stellar Military's staging area

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.630
at the Sea of the Morningstar Lagrange point,

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:28.550
then enter extra-planetary orbit.

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:30.510
But our true plan

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.310
is to head to this staging area,

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:37.690
where the Bentenmaru is moored, and board the ship.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.440
This is the Odette II's primary objective.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.820
So we can deploy the launch from the approach point, right?

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:45.200
No.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.910
I want to avoid detection by the autonomous satellites,

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.570
so we'll do it earlier.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.330
Marika!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:53.790
They say there are stowaways in the hangar!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.580
Jeez...

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.050
You really should remember you're a princess.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.720
But I consider myself a yacht club member more than a princess.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:10.220
And I was doing you a favor by not telling you

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.510
when the practice cruise would be...

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.350
Neither one of us

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.770
is particularly interested in our royal positions.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.860
My sister wishes to aid you.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.230
And we would be useful

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.820
to have around in a pinch, Captain.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:33.620
If we're done here, I'd like to prepare the launch.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.740
Chiaki, did you help them stow away?!

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:38.710
Yes.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.880
The more crew, the better.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.500
You should've told me...

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.680
President, it's time.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.680
Just another minute.

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:00.810
I could try a different format,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.730
but the Odette II's programming

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.070
prioritizes versatility and survival,

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.190
so it's a bad match.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.240
I don't want to give it any weird quirks.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.990
We want our fellow students

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.910
still running this thing in a hundred years.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.870
You sound just like Jenny.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.290
Okay...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.670
Even if the worst happens, and no one returns,

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.000
it will function autonomously.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:27.800
Let's go.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:33.930
Launching.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.930
Make sure not to get shaken off.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:36.720
Roger.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.190
Stay calm.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.600
I'm sorry.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:47.610
Sea of the Morningstar...

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:02.290
It's pretty.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.540
So that's how our ship looks.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.800
You're about to see a lot more.

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:15.720
Approaching Vessel Detected

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.720
What's up?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:20.470
The Bentenmaru has a visitor.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:22.640
I'll switch the screen over to display it.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.360
The Hakuoh Academy Yacht Club?

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.860
Does that mean Marika's heading for the Bentenmaru with the yacht club?

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.320
She may intend to board.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.360
Why?

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.320
Our pirating license.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:38.580
Misa...

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.000
Did you pack that outfit?

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.000
It's easier to blend in wearing this.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.780
So, I just picked up some information.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:47.540
Information?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.500
I overheard the nurses talking.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.090
They plan to extend our isolation by two weeks.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:58.970
I knew it.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.560
What should I do?!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.140
I'll lose even more of my edge!

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.230
More importantly, our pirating business!

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.150
We'll have to turn down a lot of jobs...

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.610
No, if we can't use the Bentenmaru for another two weeks,

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:13.490
our Letter of Marque will be revoked.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:15.320
Correct.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:20.580
Then, could Marika be trying to protect our pirating license?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.170
No way!

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.970
Misa's checking in?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:36.220
What do I do?

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:38.510
Shouldn't you answer it?

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.140
She'll be suspicious if you don't.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.450
Y-Yeah.

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.730
Hello? This is Marika!

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.140
Oh, Marika...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.310
Let's see...

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.770
Wasn't your practice cruise today?

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.190
Huh? Oh, yes!

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.030
We're practicing our spacewalks...

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:56.570
Ah, I see.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.320
How are you doing there?

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.660
Our symptoms are gone, and we're fine.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.740
We're thinking of staging a break out—

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:05.580
No! Take your time!

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:08.500
All right.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.580
Don't work too hard, okay?

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.300
We can't come get you, like last time.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.920
I know.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.050
I'm not worried.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.720
Do as you please, just don't get yourself killed.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:20.840
Yeah.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.560
Tell everyone to take care.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.770
Good luck, Captain.

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.770
She didn't say anything.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.480
I don't know how long this deception will hold,

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:34.730
but I don't want to worry them.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.660
I expected you to ask her some leading questions.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.740
Why?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:45.080
It's the captain's decision.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.500
If she isn't telling us, I'm sure she has her reasons.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.670
You're letting the captain and the yacht club

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:53.170
take the Bentenmaru?

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:54.590
That's nuts.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.130
Amateurs can't fly that thing.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.380
He's right.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:00.180
Our electronics are all customized.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.890
There's no manual. If they screw up...

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:08.100
Perhaps it will break down the moment they turn on the power.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:11.270
In that case,

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:13.900
let's make them a manual.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.190
A guide that will walk even a total piloting amateur through the steps.

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.700
Well, I guess we do have to help little Miss Marika!

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.460
They're my students too.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.120
Better than letting them guess how to use it.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.540
Now, then...

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:34.630
Okay!

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.050
I'll get a computer.

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.010
I hope we make it in time.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.660
It's big...

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:06.870
It looks bigger than our ship.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:09.120
It's actually the same length.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.750
We're about to decelerate.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.730
I'll head inside and boot it up.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.330
It's quiet.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.710
I'll start by booting up the electronics and other equipment.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.470
They're already on board...

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.850
Speed up!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.690
So this is a pirate comm seat...

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.320
I bet electronic warfare here is a lot of fun!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.650
We're not doing any.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.700
Marika, what is this chair?

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.360
No! That's...

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.710
How pretty...

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:43.960
Hold it, Haramaki!

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:45.510
What if the military had seen that?!

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:46.800
S-Sorry.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.590
I couldn't resist.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:49.350
Jeez.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.850
Guys, don't touch anything...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.940
What are they doing?

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:59.810
Let's hurry with those manuals.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.110
Now, then...

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.030
Now that we're on board, we need to get it flying.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.370
But I don't remember the exact launch procedure...

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:10.570
Glance.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.830
I don't suppose it matches the Barbalusa's...

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.330
Of course not.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.160
Naturally...

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.460
Is there a manual?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.290
I'm sure it's here somewhere.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.000
The ship's been heavily modified.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.710
A standard manual won't help.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:26.760
Yeah...

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.510
But worrying won't help, either.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:30.590
So let's try!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.810
Keep the converter reactor at low propulsion.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.190
Watch it closely, and increase the speed gradually.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.190
Set a course for extra-planetary orbit.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.530
For now, let's get some distance from Tau Ceti.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.530
Roger!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:47.610
Oh, no... They're going to launch!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.370
The propellant won't stabilize at low propulsion...

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:54.030
Impurities and ash will clog the fuel lines, and cleaning will be a nightmare!

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:54.830
I just finished writing that.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.620
How long will it take to finish, guys?

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:57.830
Five minutes.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.960
I hope the Bentenmaru makes it!

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.500
I'll have it done in two!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.920
Anyone not seated, prepare for turbulence.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.670
Now, then...

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:08.420
Launch!

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:19.600
Um...

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:22.100
The cleaning...

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.070
That's strange...

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.320
Give it another try?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.820
I think it'd just end the same way.

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:31.570
Marika, what do we do?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.770
W-Well...

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:34.830
Marika?

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:36.030
Yes?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.370
At times like this...

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.960
Eat something sweet, and think it over.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:53.090
My country has a saying: "Sweets for when you're worried."

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.100
You brought all this from the Lamp House?

00:15:55.610 --> 00:15:56.990
Since we were stowing away,

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:58.890
we thought we should bring snacks.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.850
Everyone, eat as much as you like.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.060
Thanks!

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.450
Marika, you have a message.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.290
Oh, Captain!

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:20.000
Did I interrupt snack time?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.960
P-Phow-phan!

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:23.460
P-Pardon me!

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:25.460
I thought you'd be having a more difficult time.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:26.880
I am! I am!

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:28.590
I really am having a hard time!

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:29.670
I see!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.720
Then I think I can help!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:33.800
I was going over some old files,

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.680
and I found the Bentenmaru's manual.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:36.640
Want it?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.100
Yes! Please let us have it!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.520
Then I will send it right over.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.440
Thank you!

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.440
Simple
<b>For Beginners
Bentenmaru Operating Manual</b>

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:51.990
I get it.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.900
So that's how the engine works.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.570
I wanna do some electronic warfare...

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:57.410
You shouldn't, Lynn.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.200
Okay.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.450
Marika, it's all entered...

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:02.830
We're ready too!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.540
Finished here.

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:05.920
Good here.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.040
Okay.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.750
We're fine.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.220
Let's try it again!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.630
Beta
Alpha

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.630
Launch!

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:26.770
All right!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.740
I'm glad we made it in time.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:38.910
The Bentenmaru survived...

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:40.990
I can't go on.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.750
Now we can finally resume our hanafuda card game...

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.370
Now let's do an FTL jump!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:50.630
It'll be a little difficult, but to carry out our piracy,

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.800
we'll need to jump to the enemy ship.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.800
So I think we should practice now.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:57.050
I see.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:01.470
Hey, we didn't put anything about FTL jumps in that manual...

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:03.680
If they screw up, they could blow out the engine!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:05.020
Wh-What do we do?

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:07.730
That's strange...

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.690
There's nothing in the manual that covers FTL jumps.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:13.360
Huh? There isn't?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.070
Then, should we contact the insurance company,

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.530
and ask that one be sent over?

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.410
Trouble!

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.330
Stellar Military vessel heading toward us!

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.370
They must have seen that laser blast.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.080
We need to leave at once.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.870
Are we fast enough to shake them?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:30.170
Impossible...

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:34.170
We launched at low propulsion, so the propellant hasn't stabilized.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:43.510
Marika.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.270
We'll jump.

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.610
She's nuts!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.530
But if the Stellar Alliance catches her, that'll be a problem too!

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.490
At these times, Marika usually has something up her sleeve.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:04.740
Let us have faith in our captain!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.410
The first step of an FTL jump

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.460
is knowing your exact position and coordinates.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.250
As long as you get the settings right,

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:17.420
the computer will take care of the rest automatically.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.800
Next we have to set the flight plan.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.720
This should be automatic, as well.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:30.100
The problem is the engine.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:35.190
The Bentenmaru has two converter reactors, alpha and beta.

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:38.280
But San-Daime mentioned that they're pretty old,

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.650
so they can be difficult.

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:40.150
Beta
Alpha

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.370
Specifically, it's difficult to stabilize beta's output.
Beta
Alpha

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.950
I see...

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:48.120
Converter reactors are a complicated pain in the butt to begin with.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.660
And we're using them past their life cycle?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.330
But we have a good crew to bridge the difference.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.670
I've figured out the engine.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.460
We're in a hurry this time,

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:01.300
so I think we should only use alpha for the jump.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:02.760
Yeah.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:03.680
Let's do it.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.140
Way to go, Captain!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.390
You don't need no manual.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:09.600
She's seen us do it, so she should know.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.390
It would actually be strange if she couldn't get it to launch.

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:16.570
Please, alpha... Just work like usual!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.780
Coorie, is the Stellar Military jamming working yet?

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:21.360
In progress!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.950
I'll clean you up all nice and shiny later, so please...

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.860
There they are.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:31.620
Set a course for the Cepheus dark bay.

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:32.660
Let's go.

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.370
Roger!

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.330
Faster than light jump!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:47.100
Hooray!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.720
We're in subspace!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.100
Yay!

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.480
Whew...

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:00.280
You did it, Marika...

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.320
You really do have something.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.490
What's wrong?

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:12.160
What is this?

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.340
They finally found it.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:23.090
They're two princesses and a pirate's daughter.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:25.700
Well, if they keep this up,

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:27.300
they'll be just fine.

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:36.480
It appears the crew was watching us.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.560
Oh, I see...

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.360
Then that manual...

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:44.030
That would hurt Marika's pride, so let's keep it a secret.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:46.660
You're right.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.950
Everyone! Now that we're settled in, want to eat?

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:53.700
Sounds good. What do you want?

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.750
I'd like curry.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:57.420
Sounds great!

00:21:57.740 --> 00:22:00.380
Then, let's get started!

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:02.130
Right!

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.220
Smuggling, Leaving Port, and a Leap

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:41.480
The Bentenmaru has launched successfully.

00:23:42.060 --> 00:23:44.110
But piracy is harder than they expect.

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:47.110
Careful attention and detailed procedures...

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:49.780
Will the easygoing yacht club members

00:23:49.780 --> 00:23:51.780
be able to complete the job?

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:54.950
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.440 --> 00:23:57.830
The Hakuoh Pirates' first job.

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
The Hakuoh Pirates' First Job

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.050
Phow-phan!
